@startuml @ Scripture

' This class is how the user interacts with the Scripture class.
class Program {
    + Main()
    + DisplayMenu()
}

' The Scripture class is the basically the core of how the program works.
' All the other classes use this class to create a scripture object.
class Scripture {
    - _scripture : List<Word>
    - _scriptureReference : Reference
    --
    + Scripture(reference : string, scripture : string)
    + HideRandomWords() : void
    + IsCompletelyHidden() : bool
    + GetDisplayText() : string
}

' This class is used to define what a word is. It is useful because it adds functionality of actually hiding each word.
' Every word in a scripture is an object. We need this class to hide each individual word.
' The scripture class is the only class that uses this.
class Word {
    - _text : string
    ' default to false
    - _isHidden : bool
    --
    + Word(word : string)
    + HideWord() : void
    + IsHidden() : bool
    + GetDisplayText() : string
}

' The reference class is there to display the reference of the scripture, but it's main use is to detect if the scripture has
' more than 1 verse.
' The scripture class is the only class that uses this.
class Reference {
    - _book : string
    - _chapter : string
    - _startVerse : int
    - _endVerse : int
    - _isOneVerse : bool
    --
    + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, startVerse : int)
    + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, startVerse : int, endVerse : int)
    + GetReference() : string
}

Program --> Scripture
Scripture --> Reference
Scripture --> Word

@enduml